  "research_decisions": [
    "Use only the stable v1.1.0 Ed25519 historical compatibility subset. The current C2SP recommendation for new deployments is ML-DSA; this does not select a deployment algorithm.",
    "Pin complete keys and exact origin; require the complete configured roster. Four-byte IDs and unknown signatures confer no authority.",
    "Timestamped signatures make a historical cosigner declaration, not qualified UTC, independent administration or an external latest-head floor.",
    "No Merkle proof accompanies this inspection. Existing inclusion/consistency machinery and retained predecessor binding remain separate dependencies.",
    "ArXiv 1503.08768 was discovered at abstract depth only in this tranche and is not an implementation source. The prior full research/paid-route packet remains docs/PAID_FINDINGS_DECISION_2026-10-11.md."
  ],
  "development_observations": [
    "Initial private signature exploration applied the Ed25519 identifier rule to every configuration key and stopped on an ECDSA entry. Restricted extraction to selected type-0x01 keys; no upstream key defect was established. ECDSA identifiers follow a different rule.",
    "Initial 102 owned controls passed; three additional resource/order controls bring the final focused suite to 105 on both runtimes.",
    "Sampled review of native timestamp DER tree/collection/input bounds and typed refusal handling found no new confirmed defect. This was not a complete audit or a demonstrated process-resource bound."
  ],
  "claim_boundaries": [
    "The checkpoint and key material share publisher repository custody; no independent bootstrap or administration proof.",
    "Historical timestamp claims 1729698503 and 1729698499 are retained exactly; no ambient-time freshness decision.",
    "An owned validly signed fork passes signature mathematics while consistency and latest-head flags remain false.",
    "Parser/retention caps are finite subset restrictions, not process isolation or total memory/CPU bounds.",
    "No native adapter, trust enrollment, lifecycle integration, kernel change, provider-protocol request, inclusion proof or consistency proof.",
    "Raw public captures and reports are ignored local evidence; a fresh clone lacks those bytes. Tests use repository-owned deterministic fixtures only."
  ],
